§ `S 35/2012: one Notification for all designated licensees, cancelling the first three (in operation 1 February 2012)`

-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:29 | Citation and commencement
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:30 | 1. This Notification may be cited as the Telecommunications
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:31 | (Designated Telecommunication Licensees) Notification 2012 and
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:32 | shall come into operation on 1st February 2012.
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:34 | Designated telecommunication licensees
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:35 | 2.—(1) The Authority hereby declares every telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:36 | licensee, which is granted a licence under section 5 of the Act
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:37 | to provide facilities-based operations, to be a designated
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:38 | telecommunication licensee for the purposes of Part VA of the Act.
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:39 | (2) The Authority hereby declares the following
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:40 | telecommunication licensees, each of which is granted a licence
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:41 | under section 5 of the Act to provide services-based operations,
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:42 | to be designated telecommunication licensees for the purposes
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:43 | of Part VA of the Act:
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:44 | (a) PacNet Internet (S) Pte Ltd;
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:45 | (b) Syniverse Technologies (Singapore) Pte Ltd.
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:48 | Cancellation
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:49 | 3. The following Notifications are cancelled:
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:50 | (a) the Telecommunications (Designated Telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:51 | Licensees — Facilities-based Operator) Notification 2005
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:52 | (G.N. No. S 86/2005);
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:53 | (b) the Telecommunications (Designated Telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:54 | Licensees — Services-based Operator) Notification 2005
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:55 | (G.N. No. S 233/2005);
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:56 | (c) the Telecommunications (Designated Telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:57 | Licensees — Services-based Operator) Notification 2007
-- src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:58 | (G.N. No. S 390/2007).
@ref DTL Notification 2012 (src:TA1999-DTL-S35-2012:29-58)
GIVEN `conduct day` IS A DATE
      `reading day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`DTL S 35/2012 is in operation for the conduct day, as read on the reading day` MEANS
    (`reading day` AT LEAST (Date 31 1 2012)) AND (`conduct day` AT LEAST (Date 1 2 2012))

-- Paragraph 2(1): every facilities-based operator is designated.  Before S 35/2012 it was S 86/2005 that said so; neither says anything before 4 March 2005 in any deposited text.
GIVEN `conduct day` IS A DATE
      `reading day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`DTL: every facilities-based operator is a designated telecommunication licensee for the conduct day, as read on the reading day` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `DTL S 35/2012 is in operation for the conduct day, as read on the reading day` `conduct day` `reading day` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `DTL S 86/2005 is in operation for the conduct day, as read on the reading day` `conduct day` `reading day` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `S 192/2012: amends paragraph 2(2) of S 35/2012 (in operation 11 May 2012)`

